# Generated satellite imagery is NEVER committed.
#
# Each run rewrites every product's newest frame, and a PNG is a fresh binary
# blob that git cannot delta-compress against the previous one — roughly
# 600 MB of new objects per day at the 10-minute update cadence.  Superseded
# blobs stay stored server-side even after they become unreachable, so no
# commit strategy (append, amend, or orphan force-push) bounds the repository
# size.  The frames are published to GitHub Pages as a deployment artifact
# instead; see the header of .github/workflows/main.yml.
site/data/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
